\section{Mitigation Comparison}
\label{app:mitigations}

Table~\ref{tab:mitigation_comparison} grades every mitigation the search found together with those
of Section~\ref{sec:controls}. The grade measures breadth of evidence, not effect size: A meets all of
(i) at least two model families, (ii) at least two task domains, and (iii) multi-turn or held-out
testing; B meets two; C one; D none; U marks a method proposed against sycophancy whose source
reports no sycophancy measurement. Methods neither proposed against nor evaluated on sycophancy,
including Constitutional AI~\citep{bai2022constitutional} and representation
editing~\citep{kong2024repredit}, are omitted. Every grade comes from a full-text reading recorded
with quotes in the artifact.

